From 8cb59625d3100d9c27a4ad48c44ff48cccb83026 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ashhart <71890694+ashhart@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:36:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] flashnext cuda: hold two graphs per window graph cache slot

A Flash Next window pass alternates between a stream's state and its
spare from round to round, and its head inputs alternate too, so the
one-graph-per-slot cache re-recorded the slot's graph almost every
round. Each slot now holds two graphs with least-recently-used
eviction: a round replays a graph only when its whole key (pointers,
sizes and shapes) matches, otherwise the second way is captured or the
older one is re-recorded in place. The total stays capped at 128 held
graphs. Kernels, arguments and replies are unchanged; only how often a
graph is captured changes.
